description: Folder layout and one-way dependency flow for Next.js App Router + Supabase
alwaysApply: true
---

# Architecture

Colocate by feature, separate by layer. Route folders own UI. Business logic, data access, and types live outside `app/`. Nothing talks to Supabase from a component.

## Folders (project root)

- `app/` — routes only (pages, layouts, route handlers, one-off route UI)
- `components/` — shared UI (`ui/` primitives, `[feature]/` reused widgets)
- `lib/` — infra only (Supabase clients, utils, third-party SDKs)
- `data/` — reads (SELECT)
- `actions/` — Server Actions (INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE)
- `types/` — shared TypeScript types
- `validations/` — Zod schemas (client + server)
- `hooks/` — custom React hooks
- `stores/` — Zustand only. Do not create this folder or install Zustand until client global state cannot live in Server Components or URL search params. Never Redux.
- `constants/` — enums, route paths, flags
- `middleware.ts` — Next.js middleware
- `supabase/migrations/` — append-only SQL (never edit applied/merged files)

## Dependency flow (one direction)

```
app/  →  actions/, data/  →  lib/  →  Supabase
  ↓
components/, hooks/  →  types/, validations/, constants/
```

- Components and hooks never import Supabase
- `data/` and `actions/` never import from `app/`
- `lib/supabase/admin.ts` only from server-only files (`actions/`, `app/api/`)

`data/` (reads during render) and `actions/` (writes from forms) stay separate. They are service + repository in one — do not add a extra repository layer unless we swap databases later.
